+Files
+*****
+
+``zvfs_sync()`` writes the buffered data of every open regular file to its
+backing store, as ``zvfs_fsync()`` does for one descriptor. Descriptions of
+other kinds have nothing to flush and are not visited: a pipe or socket read
+holds its description for as long as it waits. The call always completes.
+Data held only by a memory mapping is written back by ``zvfs_msync()``,
+described below.
